"text":"\" minus the number of closing parentheses \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". For example, the balance of the sequence \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(()(("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is 3."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A balanced parentheses sequence can also be defined as a parentheses sequence with balance 0 such that each of its prefixes has a non-negative balance."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We define the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balanced shuffle"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation that takes a parentheses sequence and returns a parentheses sequence as follows: first, for every character of the input sequence, we compute the balance of the prefix of the sequence "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"before"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" that character and write those down in a table together with the positions of the characters in the input sequence, for example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prefix balance"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children